WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:06.560
When I first started our financial firm back
in October of '09, one of the biggest concerns

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.910
that we had originally was how we were going
to compete against these other guys we were

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.809
competing against when they've raised tens
of millions of dollars and we didn't have

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:16.090
any money to raise.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.580
It was all my money that we started off with.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.940
How can we compete against these guys?

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.940
And we lost several agents initially when
we started the company because they all came

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:28.410
and looked at me in my eyes and they said,
"Pat, you're going to go out of business.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.810
Everyone is going to be affected by this.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.790
It's the biggest mistake you're making.

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:33.360
You shouldn't be doing this.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.750
It's going to hurt a lot of people.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:35.750
But I stuck around.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:37.540
Why did I stick around?

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:44.149
Because in my gut, I did not believe that
financial capital was the most important form

00:00:44.149 --> 00:00:47.629
of capital and I'll explain to you here in
a minute why that is.

00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:49.249
I didn't believe that.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:53.420
In reality, there's 9 forms of capital and
I believe one of them is the most important

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.480
one, but I'm going to explain to you what
are these different forms of capital and how

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.260
it helps you as the entrepreneur.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:01.429
So, first of all, the one we hear about all
the time is what?

00:01:01.429 --> 00:01:03.309
We hear about financial capital.

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:04.309
Right?

00:01:04.309 --> 00:01:05.309
We always hear about financial capital.

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:10.600
Most people ask me, "Hey Pat, I feel like
the reason why I can't be a business owner

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.580
is because I don't know how to raise a million
bucks.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.720
I don't know how to raise ten million dollars.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.250
How do I raise five million dollars?

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.810
How do I raise a half a million dollars?

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.280
I need a lot of financial capital."

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.310
Well, when there are people who start off
with a lot of money, say the person has a

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:30.240
lot of money, and they may have the money,
they may have a decent idea, but they have

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.910
the money, there is not that level of urgency.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.670
But that is one form of capital.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:37.430
We'll get back to that here in a minute.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.070
The next one you don't hear about a lot, I'm
going to explain to you what this means is

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:41.750
spiritual capital.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:42.750
What is spiritual capital?

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.030
What are you talking about, spiritual capital?

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:47.490
It's literally what it means.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:55.700
Spiritual capital is when a community is targeting
a product that they are from that faith base,

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.130
from that religion.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:04.410
There's a lot of product in entrepreneurship
that are tied to a certain faith, to a certain

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:10.670
religion, and that person has an advantage
because they know exactly how that faith thinks

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:16.000
or how that community and that religion thinks
so that's what you call spiritual capital.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Next one is land capital.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.920
Let me explain to you what land capital is.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:26.120
Land capital is let's just say for instance
you have 10 acres of land in Napa Valley -- hypothetically.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:30.660
Your grandparents had it, they left it to
you, and you want to start a wine company.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:35.220
Well, you happen to have the land in a prime
location that's for what?

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.220
Wine.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.220
Why?

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.160
Because the key to making the best type of
wine is what?

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.420
The biggest difference in temperature.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:45.500
The key to making the best type of wine is
the biggest difference in temperature, meaning

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.690
it goes very high, and then it goes very low.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:51.820
That's exactly why Napa Valley is a prime
location for land.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.880
And that's exactly what land capital is.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:57.930
Your edge when you're negotiating with somebody
else is that you happen to have 10 acres of

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.860
land in such and such place.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:00.860
Okay?

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:06.500
I happen to have 100 acres of land in such
and such and such place that we've never dug

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:13.599
for oil, never have, and within a 10-mile
radius 17 different people have and they've

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:14.749
started.

00:03:14.749 --> 00:03:16.490
. . whatever you may be saying.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:18.270
But that's land capital.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.819
Next one is social capital.

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:21.569
Social capital is a cause.

00:03:21.569 --> 00:03:22.690
A crusade.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:28.520
A group of 50, 100, 200 people that have bought
into a cause.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:32.480
And they want to do something about this cause
to make a difference around the world.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.750
You cannot buy social capital.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:39.120
But social capital is from the heart, social
capital comes from feelings.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.739
Social capital comes from I have to make sure
we correct an injustice.

00:03:42.739 --> 00:03:45.220
I have to make sure this becomes a reality.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.590
That's one sort of social capital.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:51.100
So, a lot of companies would love to invest
in social capital.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.100
Why?

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.900
Because their biggest problem is social capital.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.190
It's their biggest problem.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:59.280
Land capital, they can always buy the land
if they wanted to.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.310
You know, spiritual capital is one you need
this if you want to get into this, but it's

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:06.070
a very small minute community of people.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:08.060
The next one is cultural capital.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.209
What is cultural capital?

00:04:09.209 --> 00:04:19.470
So for instance, you come to me and you say,
"Hey Patrick, I know this product we created

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:26.030
and this is mainly tailored towards the Filipino
Tagalog speaking community because this is

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.100
. . . And I understand their culture.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.060
It's very similar to the spiritual, but it's
more cultural.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:34.780
I'm going to focus on the cultural side and
I know exactly what they need.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:35.780
No problem.

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:40.470
In this family, the way they do their weddings
is a three-day wedding and we wanted to start

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:45.160
a business because there is this business
in India where it focused on the Indian community,

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:50.051
on how their weddings are done and we specialize
in this and this is what we have and all of

00:04:50.051 --> 00:04:52.650
our products are imports, so anybody that
wants to do the wedding, here for the three

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:58.000
days we do this, this, this and the package
is $50,000 and if we do 50 weddings a year,

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.600
that's 2.5 million dollar revenue.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.800
If we do 500, it 25 million dollars.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:07.600
And there's this many people that get married
in America, the Indian population is let's

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:12.200
just say 6.5 million people and 6.5 million
people, there's this many people between these

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:16.610
ages, so we're projecting there's going to
be one million marriages in the next whatever

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:19.060
and let's just say 50%.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.660
. . so that's the calculation, cultural.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:22.660
Got it.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:23.660
You make your argument for that.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:25.330
The next type of capital is experiential capital.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.330
What is that?

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:29.460
I'm starting a technology company and I have
experience in technology.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.949
I don't have any money to start it with, but
I've worked at Google, I've worked at Facebook,

00:05:32.949 --> 00:05:38.050
I've worked with Zuckerberg, I was his number
seven engineer, when Facebook first got started,

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:40.310
I know exactly what's going on over here and
I've got experience.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.350
I'm just, you know, hypothetical.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:47.620
I have experience in how to work with this
area and what I know is weapons very well,

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:52.220
and I think with the gun laws that are taking
place, and all these challenges that are going

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:55.650
on in America, I'm very good at selling guns
and I understand who needs it and I know that

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:57.380
community and I have a lot of experience - whatever.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:02.639
I mean, this sounds weird things I'm throwing
out there to you because there's so many ways

00:06:02.639 --> 00:06:05.570
to make money in business.

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:06.570
Intellectual capital.

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:07.570
What's intellectual capital?

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.169
It's simply intellectual capital.

00:06:09.169 --> 00:06:15.449
We're talking about patents you may have,
we're talking about trademarks you may have,

00:06:15.449 --> 00:06:21.860
we're talking about know-how, knowledge, we're
talking about wisdom, but it's intellectual

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:22.960
capital that they have in that area.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.449
Then the next one is natural capital.

00:06:25.449 --> 00:06:26.650
What is natural capital?

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:29.850
We're talking about renewable energy.

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:32.901
We're talking about things like that that
is natural capital.

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:35.729
And then obviously, it's material.

00:06:35.729 --> 00:06:37.090
What's material?

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:40.509
Tools, machinery, things like that are material
capital.

00:06:40.509 --> 00:06:43.699
This is all different forms of capital.

00:06:43.699 --> 00:06:48.130
Most people think the most important type
of capital is financial.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.320
Again, I said this at the beginning.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:52.450
Most people think this is the most important
form of capital.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:56.620
You've got to ask yourself which form of capital
you have.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:07:01.630
So if you yourself need this [financial],
you better have one of these.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:04.389
By the way, this [financial] is the easiest
one to get.

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:05.500
Just so you know.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:07.460
It's the easiest one to get.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:10.199
If you want this [financial], you better have
one of these other forms of capital.

00:07:10.199 --> 00:07:13.980
So what case are you making as you're trying
to raise your money?

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:17.259
If you want to raise your money from a company
and say I need a quarter million dollars,

00:07:17.259 --> 00:07:18.259
why?

00:07:18.259 --> 00:07:21.100
Let me tell you what intellectual capital
I have.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.479
I have patents on the following three items.

00:07:23.479 --> 00:07:24.720
Okay, great.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:25.720
Awesome.

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:26.720
What else?

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:31.889
I have experience because I worked with . . . . and
I know how to do . . . . Okay, great.

00:07:31.889 --> 00:07:32.889
What else?

00:07:32.889 --> 00:07:37.440
And the market I'm trying to connect with
is such and such market and I fully understand

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:41.150
Silicon Valley culture because I've lived
there for the last 19 years.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:42.990
Okay, sounds good.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:45.570
So that's the questions they [financial] are
going to be asking and you've got to have

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:46.639
an argument for it.

00:07:46.639 --> 00:07:49.220
Another one could be, I need to raise some
money.

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:50.220
How much money do you want?

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:51.220
A half a million dollars.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:52.340
Why should we give you a half a million dollars?

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.960
Perfect question you ask.

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:55.720
Let me explain to you why it is.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:08:05.009
One, I have 7,800 people that are part of
my network who all are soccer moms and want

00:08:05.009 --> 00:08:11.289
their kids to have uniforms for soccer and
they don't like the uniform that they're currently

00:08:11.289 --> 00:08:15.130
buying from everywhere because their skin
itches and it gives them a rash.

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:22.300
And I have found this such and such material
from whatever place that is an anti-itch and

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:26.389
it's comfortable with kids' skin and it can
work with any type of skin and it's more gentle

00:08:26.389 --> 00:08:31.230
on them and our competition are the five different
companies, they're going to be doing this.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:36.250
These 7,000 soccer moms that I sit as the
chairman of the board for these 7,000 soccer

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:41.420
moms in the community of whatever state it
is, every one of them has already told me

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:42.420
they're interested.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:44.860
And if I come out with one, they're very interested
in that.

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:46.110
So here's what I have.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:49.350
I have these five women that are wanting to
help out with this.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:52.140
They're all in different chapters of this.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.140
I have social capital.

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:56.510
Then they're going to ask, do you really know
what you're talking about?

00:08:56.510 --> 00:09:00.589
I brought somebody who has intellectual -- they're
the ones with the uniform.

00:09:00.589 --> 00:09:05.150
And I brought somebody who has experience
because this woman that I'm talking to, her

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:06.150
expertise is fabric.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:08.060
She's been in the fabric business for 28 years.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:10.440
And she knows what's the best form of fabric
to have.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:14.140
Nike uses this, Under Armour uses it, this
one uses it.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:18.400
The fabric Under Armour and Nike use, they
quadrupled the cost because they have names,

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:22.360
and we don't have a name but we can start
our own specifically for kids and our Under

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:24.600
Armour was more for football when they first
got started.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.399
Nike was for runners, ours is going to be
mainly for kids.

00:09:27.399 --> 00:09:29.230
I'm again, just throwing ideas out there.

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:30.520
You may be saying, Pat, that's a great idea.

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:31.520
Great.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:32.520
That's an idea.

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:34.310
THEN you go get this [financial].

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:36.150
Now, let's work backwards.

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:41.470
Some of you guys messaged me and you say,
"Pat, I have 20 million dollars and I'm part

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:45.390
of a C fund, I'm part of this you know, small
little fund that I started myself.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:49.140
I think Kobe today announced that he's doing
100 million dollars himself, but let's just

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:50.690
say you have 20 million dollars.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:55.750
Many of my LinkedIn audience asked me this
question - Pat, I have several million, where

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:57.201
should I invest, can we partner with you?

00:09:57.201 --> 00:09:59.760
These are the questions that come up.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:00.760
Perfect.

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:03.550
If you're on the financial capital side, your
struggle isn't money.

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:07.400
Either you have the money because of the sale
of a company, you were part of a company,

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:11.380
the company went public, you had shares, you
made seven million bucks.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.600
Or you made four million dollars, three million
dollars.

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:16.670
The death of a family, you have 17 million
dollars.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:18.201
You had inheritance that came to you.

00:10:18.201 --> 00:10:21.790
You have your parents that left their will
or trust to you, right?

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:24.649
You could have something where a contract
from sports.

00:10:24.649 --> 00:10:28.160
Several NBA players follow me on LinkedIn
and send me messages about this.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.709
What do I do with a big contract that I just
got?

00:10:30.709 --> 00:10:31.709
Perfect.

00:10:31.709 --> 00:10:34.890
You're here [financial], then you got to look
at this [other capital] on which one makes

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:40.610
sense to you, but for you, as you're assessing
what companies to invest in, you've got to

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:43.899
ask the question, what type of material capital
do you have?

00:10:43.899 --> 00:10:46.790
I'm sorry, they don't know what material capital
is.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.010
Next question.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:51.021
Do you have any type of natural capital?

00:10:51.021 --> 00:10:52.021
No.

00:10:52.021 --> 00:10:53.021
Any type of intellectual capital?

00:10:53.021 --> 00:10:54.021
Yes.

00:10:54.021 --> 00:10:55.021
What is it?

00:10:55.021 --> 00:10:56.021
. . . okay, that's good.

00:10:56.021 --> 00:10:57.021
Do you have the patent on that?

00:10:57.021 --> 00:10:58.021
Yes, it's pending right now.

00:10:58.021 --> 00:10:59.021
When did you post it?

00:10:59.021 --> 00:11:00.021
Six months ago.

00:11:00.021 --> 00:11:01.021
Okay.

00:11:01.021 --> 00:11:02.510
What type of experiential capital do you have?

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:05.209
Oh, my cousin used to work at Google.

00:11:05.209 --> 00:11:07.100
My cousin used to work at Goldman Sachs.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.410
My cousin whatever.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:12.110
My best friend just graduated from Harvard
and he's got four buddies.

00:11:12.110 --> 00:11:13.110
Good.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:14.110
Next.

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.110
Cultural.

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:16.110
What cultural connection do you have?

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:17.110
I'm a millennial.

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:18.110
What's your point?

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:19.110
There are so many millennials.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:21.080
Let me tell you what type of a millennial
I am.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:23.690
I totally understand the nightclub life right
now.

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:27.720
I totally understand what vibes at nightclubs
and what kind of music, I'm in the EDM community.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:29.770
I know everyone in the EDM world.

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:32.290
I listen to EDM, I know EDM.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:33.770
Okay, great, where are you going with this?

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:38.330
Well the EDM community typically likes this
at the clubs and the raves and the parties

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:39.380
and whatever it is.

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:40.640
And these are the seven things.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.390
And we wanted to start something that's tailored
to that because this, this, this.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:45.940
So that's cultural.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:50.920
What's social, what's spiritual, what's land
capital, then make your decision.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:54.970
So it's very, very important to know this,
but keep this in mind.

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:59.140
This [financial] is very, very, very, very,
very easy to get.

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:02.120
Very easy to get.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:04.829
That is so easy to get.

00:12:04.829 --> 00:12:05.829
Okay?

00:12:05.829 --> 00:12:07.120
Very, very easy to get.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:10.230
Most people won't get it because their approach
-- maybe another time we'll do a video on

